{"type":"text","timestamp":1792512151550,"sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","part":{"id":"prt_15a0cc858001pLQFUtIF6c3QDM","messageID":"msg_15a0bef43001DRbDlUoMBKjOh4","sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","type":"text","text":"\n\nNow I understand the setup. Let me examine the key details:\n- The invariant: a DFS forest is valid iff it has no forward-cross edge (edge `u->v` with `discover[u] < discover[v]` where `v` is not a strict descendant of `u`), and it spans exactly the reachable set.\n- `work_ratio = candidate_work / offline_work`, where offline = full DFS recompute on **every** op. So no-op updates (return state unchanged) drive the ratio well below 1.\n\nLet me check the CLI `check` command signature and the config for this workspace:\n\n","time":{"start":1792512149592,"end":1792512151544}}}
