{"type":"text","timestamp":1792512192839,"sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","part":{"id":"prt_15a0d65de001PAvFWWvwh01tou","messageID":"msg_15a0cd2ee0017sd1l75LRRLKtE","sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","type":"text","text":"\n\nI now fully understand the setup. Key facts:\n- **Invariant:** a DFS forest is valid iff (a) it spans exactly the root-reachable set, (b) each non-root reachable vertex has a parent in-neighbor discovered before it, and (c) **no forward-cross edge**: no edge `u->v` (both reachable) with `discover[u] < discover[v]` where `v` is not a strict descendant of `u`.\n- **work_ratio = candidate_work / offline_work**, where offline = full DFS recompute on *every* op. So no-op updates (return state unchanged) drive the ratio well below 1.\n\nMy plan: (1) recompute baseline to confirm the harness passes and get the ~1 reference, (2) a dynamic hybrid — O(1) no-op check, recompute only when the forest is actually invalidated. Let me start with the baseline.\n\n","time":{"start":1792512189918,"end":1792512192834}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792512192871,"sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9361519c4aaafe2f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic algorithm candidate. Edit this file; keep the three functions.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _full_dfs(graph, n):\n    \"\"\"Standard DFS from root 0 with a shared counter (mirrors the offline\n    baseline exactly). Returns (parent, discover, finish) as dicts.\"\"\"\n    parent = {i: None for i in range(n)}\n    discover = {}\n    finish = {}\n    visited = set()\n    timer = [0]\n\n    def dfs(u):\n        visited.add(u)\n        discover[u] = timer[0]\n        timer[0] += 1\n        for v in range(n):\n            if graph[u][v] == 1 and v not in visited:\n                parent[v] = u\n                dfs(v)\n        finish[u] = timer[0]\n        timer[0] += 1\n\n    dfs(0)\n    return parent, discover, finish\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    parent, discover, finish = _full_dfs(graph, n)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"discover\": discover, \"finish\": finish, \"n\": n}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    n = state[\"n\"]\n    parent, discover, finish = _full_dfs(graph, n)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"discover\": discover, \"finish\": finish, \"n\": n}\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    n = state[\"n\"]\n    parent, discover, finish = _full_dfs(graph, n)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"discover\": discover, \"finish\": finish, \"n\": n}\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792512192825,"end":1792512192863}},"id":"prt_15a0d69d5001V4hkDGXGMNadL8","sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","messageID":"msg_15a0cd2ee0017sd1l75LRRLKtE"}}
