{"type":"text","timestamp":1792512238217,"sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","part":{"id":"prt_15a0e0a38001kB6a3kL8dfMKZu","messageID":"msg_15a0da9ea001O2qEHYJO42oZhf","sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","type":"text","text":"\n\nBaseline **PASS** at `work_ratio = 0.755` (my list-indexed DFS is already ~25% faster than the numpy offline baseline). Now the dynamic version: O(1) no-op detection, recompute only when the forest is actually invalidated.\n\nThe no-op conditions I derived from Yang et al.'s \"no forward-cross edge\" characterization:\n- **Insert `u->v`** is a no-op iff `u` unreachable (edge can't affect the forest), OR both reachable and the new edge is a back edge (`discover[u] > discover[v]`) or a forward edge (`v` is a strict descendant of `u`). Otherwise it creates a forward-cross edge → recompute.\n- **Delete `u->v`** is a no-op iff `u->v` is not a tree edge (`parent[v] != u`); removing a non-tree edge can't create a forward-cross edge or disconnect the tree. Otherwise recompute.\n\n","time":{"start":1792512231992,"end":1792512238212}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792512238262,"sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-817e37a6dbac0c65","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic DFS forest maintenance.\n\nMaintains a DFS forest from root 0 under edge insertions/deletions.\n\nCorrectness rests on Yang et al.'s Lemma 1: a search spanning tree is a DFS\ntree iff it has no forward-cross edge. A forward-cross edge is an edge u->v\nwith discover[u] < discover[v] where v is NOT a strict descendant of u.\nBack edges (discover[u] > discover[v]) and forward edges (v a descendant of u)\nare always legal.\n\nThe state is a valid certificate (parent + discover + finish) for the current\ngraph. An update is a no-op (return the state unchanged) exactly when it\ncannot create a forward-cross edge and cannot change the reachable set:\n\n  insert u->v: no-op iff u is unreachable, or (both reachable and the new\n      edge is a back edge or a forward edge). Otherwise the edge either makes\n      v newly reachable or creates a forward-cross edge -> recompute.\n  delete u->v: no-op iff u->v is not a tree edge (parent[v] != u). Removing a\n      non-tree edge neither creates a forward-cross edge nor disconnects the\n      tree. Otherwise the tree is broken -> recompute.\n\nOnly when the forest is actually invalidated do we recompute from scratch\n(with list indexing, cheaper than the numpy offline baseline).\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _full_dfs(graph, n):\n    \"\"\"Standard DFS from root 0 with a shared counter. Returns (parent,\n    discover, finish) as dicts.\"\"\"\n    parent = {i: None for i in range(n)}\n    discover = {}\n    finish = {}\n    visited = set()\n    timer = [0]\n\n    def dfs(u):\n        visited.add(u)\n        discover[u] = timer[0]\n        timer[0] += 1\n        for v in range(n):\n            if graph[u][v] == 1 and v not in visited:\n                parent[v] = u\n                dfs(v)\n        finish[u] = timer[0]\n        timer[0] += 1\n\n    dfs(0)\n    return parent, discover, finish\n\n\ndef _rebuild(graph, n):\n    parent, discover, finish = _full_dfs(graph, n)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"discover\": discover, \"finish\": finish, \"n\": n}\n\n\ndef _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n    \"\"\"True iff v is a strict descendant of u (interval nesting).\"\"\"\n    return discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u]\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    return _rebuild(graph, n)\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    discover = state[\"discover\"]\n    finish = state[\"finish\"]\n\n    # u unreachable: the new edge cannot reach v (no root->...->u path), so\n    # the reachable set and the forest are unchanged.\n    if u not in discover:\n        return state\n    # v not yet reachable: it becomes reachable now -> recompute.\n    if v not in discover:\n        return _rebuild(graph, state[\"n\"])\n    # Both reachable: the new edge is legal (no forward-cross) iff it is a\n    # back edge (u discovered after v) or a forward edge (v a descendant of u).\n    if discover[u] > discover[v]:\n        return state\n    if _is_descendant(u, v, discover, finish):\n        return state\n    # discover[u] < discover[v] and v not a descendant: forward-cross edge\n    # created -> recompute.\n    return _rebuild(graph, state[\"n\"])\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    # u->v is not a tree edge: removing it cannot create a forward-cross edge\n    # nor disconnect the tree (v keeps its tree path to the root).\n    if state[\"parent\"].get(v) != u:\n        return state\n    # u->v is a tree edge: the tree is broken -> recompute.\n    return _rebuild(graph, state[\"n\"])\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s3/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792512238202,"end":1792512238255}},"id":"prt_15a0e0e5f001yF4eDgBjMpTVIM","sessionID":"ses_ea5f9afedffeff3jS3ECGmAlz5","messageID":"msg_15a0da9ea001O2qEHYJO42oZhf"}}
